msgid "Override 1: the policies. ODRL 2.2 lets each policy declare a conflict strategy with :  (permissions override prohibitions),  (prohibitions override permissions) or  (the policy is void if any conflict is detected). These terms were checked against the ODRL 2.2 vocabulary and the pinned JSON-LD context (folio-assistant-core ). When every applicable policy declares the same strategy, the table uses it. A policy that declares none counts as , the owner's default D. If the applicable policies declare different strategies,  is . ODRL 2.2 says a policy with several conflict values (after a merge or inheritance) is void when its rules conflict (W3C ODRL Information Model 2.2, Policy Conflict Strategy). This IG treats the applicable policies of one request as merged. The only declaration that changes an outcome is  declared by every applicable policy. ODRL's own default when nothing is declared is , but the outcome is the same: with a conflict,  voids the policy and  denies, and both are refused."
