msgid "UDAP route (owner approval, 2026-10-30 20:28Z). UDAP is used as profiled by HL7 Security for Scalable Registration, Authentication, and Authorization (SSRAA),  2.0.0 (STU 2, canonical ), the IG that VHL's OAuth with SSRAA Option names. Its trust is X.509: the client's certificate chains to an anchor of a trust community, so a national X.509 PKI can serve as the anchor without GDHCN. SSRAA section numbers were read from the IG source (, tag , commit ): they follow its page order, and they agree with the IG's own cross-references, which is also how ITI-YY5 cites them (\"SSRAA Sections 2 and 3\", \"Section 5.2.1\"). The rendered pages at hl7.org were not reachable to check. SSRAA 2.0.0 is US realm; the source's  branch now builds a universal-realm successor,  3.0.0 (STU 3 post-ballot CI build), not yet published. ‡ marks a section of a UDAP.org specification (UDAP Dynamic Client Registration STU1, UDAP Server Metadata STU1, UDAP JWT-Based Client Authentication STU1) as SSRAA links it; udap.org was not reachable to check it."
msgstr ""

